<title>USA: No major cold seen in Brazil coffee belt -WSC.</title>
<headline>No major cold seen in Brazil coffee belt -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON MASS. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee regions face no threat of cold in the next few days, with low temperatures of 53-66 degrees expected, independent forecaster Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>No major cold is foreseen over the weekend, when temperatures should be near to above normal.</p>
</text>
